A shopkeeper buys an article for ₹1,200 and marks it at ₹1,500. He then gives a 10% discount on the marked price. What is his profit percentage?
A) 10%
B) 12.5%
C) 15%
D) 20%
cost = 1200
selling price is 10% discount of 1500
 10% of 1500 = 150
selling price = 1500-150
              = 1350
 profit=1350-1200
        = 150
profit % = 150/1200 *100
          = 12.5%

Answer: B) 12.5%
